UPDATE tarot_cards 
SET meaning_upright = 'GENERAL ARCHETYPE: The Seven of Wands represents the absolute archetype of "Sovereign Defensiveness"—the point at which the individual, having achieved public recognition and established a high-value position (the Six), must now exert maximum, focused effort to defend that hard-won territory against the inevitable pressures of external competition and envy. Moving beyond the celebratory triumph of the previous phase, the Seven signifies the transition to "High-Stakes Vigilance," where the sovereign consciousness is no longer focused on expansion, but on the maintenance of its established boundary against a mounting, multi-directional threat. Visually depicted as a figure standing on elevated ground, wielding a single staff to repel six others attacking from below, this archetype embodies the concept of "Positioned Integrity"—the understanding that you are currently the "standard-bearer" for your vision, and that your ability to maintain your ground, despite significant external pressure, is the ultimate measure of your commitment to your truth. Within the complex architecture of your psyche, this is the stage of "systemic hardening," where you are forced to synthesize your diverse experiences into a single, unbreakable core of purpose. When the Seven of Wands appears, your system is registering a "Defense Mode" status; your current operational environment is testing the structural durability of your vision. This card commands you to stand your ground with absolute, unwavering resolve. You are being tasked with the essential work of "principled resistance": you are not merely fighting for "ego-space," but for the integrity of the mission you have manifested. You must filter out the noise, identify the highest-priority threats to your core mandate, and exert your energy with surgical, focused intensity, refusing to be drawn into low-vibration, distracting skirmishes. To inhabit the Seven of Wands is to master the art of "centered conviction," understanding that the pressure you are under is not a sign of failure, but a direct indicator of the value and impact of the territory you occupy. It is the cosmic affirmation that you possess the necessary power to withstand the siege, provided you remain absolutely tethered to the sovereign truth that initiated your journey in the first place.',
meaning_reversed = 'GENERAL ARCHETYPE: When the Seven of Wands appears in the reversed position, it acts as a high-intensity signal of "systemic boundary collapse," "exhaustion-induced surrender," or the catastrophic failure to maintain your sovereign position against the pressures of the external field. The reversal suggests that you are currently failing to hold your ground, not because the opposition is overwhelming, but because your internal resolve—your connection to your core mission—has been hollowed out by fear, indecision, or a debilitating lack of self-belief. You are essentially "leaking your defenses," running a high-priority, high-cost maintenance script that attempts to project an image of "holding on" while you are, in reality, experiencing a profound, systemic retreat. You are over-extended, reacting to every external challenge with erratic, low-vibration counter-measures, and in your desperation to avoid being "overwhelmed," you are actually making yourself more vulnerable by abandoning your core, centered strategy. This creates a massive, systemic misalignment: you are intellectually and behaviorally attempting to perform the role of the "defender," while internally, you are actively seeking the exit, leading to a profound, chronic state of depletion, social anxiety, and a persistent, gnawing sense of impending defeat. From an analytical perspective, this is a clear sign that you are leaking your life force into a "feedback loop of capitulation"; you are prioritizing the relief of stopping the fight over the importance of protecting the territory of your soul-truth. The reversed Seven of Wands exposes the hidden, egoic fear that drives this behavior: the paralyzing terror of being truly defeated, and the corresponding fear that your conviction was never actually as strong as you projected. This reversal commands an immediate, radical intervention: you must stop the output of these reactive, performative scripts, perform a brutal audit of your current defensive infrastructure, and confront the reality of why you are so hesitant to stand for your own vision. It is a demand to stop the self-deception that keeps you tethered to a failing defense, and to initiate the move toward a genuine, humble, and often terrifying reclamation of your own, individual authority. You are being tasked with the uncomfortable, yet essential, work of core-reconstruction—accepting that the "stuckness" you feel is the direct result of having prioritized the comfort of "giving up" over the responsibility of "defending," and realizing that until you are willing to plant your feet and speak your truth with absolute, centered power, you will continue to be overrun by the very chaos you have allowed to enter your perimeter.'
WHERE id = 21;
